    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0353" n="279" xml:id="pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/750</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-01T21:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 1, 1917, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 4, 2.15
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2050. Judson saw Trotsky to-day with my approval as at yesterday’s meeting of
                    Allied chiefs I advocated unofficial effort to influence armistice terms at
                    conference beginning to-morrow. No objection was offered to each chief’s
                    exerting such influence unofficially and not personally. Judson making full
                    report to War Department.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d266-f1"/> Says no friction
                    attended first session and thinks some good accomplished. My desire was as
                    indicated my 2039, November 28, 12 noon,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d266-f2"/> to
                    throw safeguards around separate armistice, if inevitable, that would protect
                    other fronts and prevent transfer thereto of German troops now confronting
                    Russian Army; also to prevent liberation of Austrian-German prisoners and
                    Russian prisoners. Trotsky told Judson had thought of such provisos.</p>
                <p>Allied chiefs still carefully avoiding recognition. Reports continue that
                    Bolsheviki will not have majority in Assembly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
